{
  "item": "DeathCow01",
  "mu_name": "Death Cow",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain's MONSTER_MODEL_DEATH_COW = 30, so OpenMonsterModel loads Monster31.bmd; the server's type is MONSTER_DEATH_COW = 41. The client's name is 데쓰 카우 (ZzzCharacter.cpp:13842-13849). OpenMU's Version075 LostTower.cs:887-917 names number 41 'Death Cow' at level 57 with 4500 health, 170-180 damage, 110 defense, MoveRange 3, AttackRange 1, ViewRange 7, AttackDelay 1600, no AttackSkill. 51 spots: 32 on Lost Tower 3, 19 on 4.",
  "world": "losttower",
  "object_type": 41,
  "monster": {
    "model_index": 30,
    "scale": 1.1
  },
  "monster_from": "ZzzCharacter.cpp:13842-13849, CreateMonster, case MONSTER_DEATH_COW: `c->Weapon[0].Type = MODEL_GREAT_HAMMER; c->Object.Scale = 1.1f;` (Level 1 commented out). No BlendMesh, no HiddenMesh.",
  "right_hand": "Mace04",
  "right_hand_bone": "left_bone",
  "right_hand_from": "MODEL_GREAT_HAMMER is Item/Mace04.bmd (new here). Its bone is CreateCharacter's weapon switch, the Bull Fighter's: `case MODEL_BULL_FIGHTER: case MODEL_DEATH_COW: c->Weapon[0].LinkBone = 42; c->Weapon[1].LinkBone = 33` (ZzzCharacter.cpp:12045-12048). Bone 42 is left_bone on this rig too, the artist's name the wrong way round as on the Bull Fighter.",
  "profile": "monster",
  "rig_from": "Seven actions, slots 0 to 6, exported with --actions=0,1,2,3,4,5,6. Keys: 20, 30, 7, 8, 8, 12, 12. 45 bones, the Bull Fighter's names: smok_bone (24), top_bone02 and top_bone01 (22, 23), left_bone (42), right_bone01 (33). BoneHead = 20, Bip01 Head (ZzzOpenData.cpp:3387). OpenMonsterModel's default play speeds; 30 is not in the override list.",
  "sheets": {
    "wwo": "deathcow_wwo.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "One sheet, Data/Monster/wwo.OZJ, 128 by 128, no alpha, on all 1109 triangles. Decoded under a deathcow_ prefix.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "wwo": "bone"
  },
  "sheet_materials_from": "Read off the sheet at 2x: a horned bovine skull, a human skull, ribbed plates and a clawed hand, all in the same weathered brown-bone -- an armour of bones, so bone.",
  "effects_from": "Two of the client's, both by name in game/play_open.cpp. RenderEye(o, 22, 23) for MODEL_DEATH_COW always (ZzzCharacter.cpp:11209-11211), the Elite Bull Fighter's red eyes (fx/eyes.h). And CharacterDie's case (:1480-1486): `o->Live = false`, MODEL_BONE1 and ten MODEL_BONE2, PlayBuffer(SOUND_BONE2) -- it comes apart into bones as the skeletons do (Bones::burst). The Bull Fighter's snort is MODEL_BULL_FIGHTER's case alone; the Death Cow does not snort.",
  "sounds_from": "ZzzOpenData.cpp:3380-3387: the Bull Fighter's mBull1/2, mBullAttack1/2 and mBullDie, SetMonsterSound(..., 0, 1, 2, 3, 4). Wired as deathcow_*; its die is mBone2, the SOUND_BONE2 CharacterDie plays as the bones fly, since the body is gone before a death clip could cry.",
  "islands_from": "23 islands for 1109 triangles, all bone: the sheet is one weathered armour of skulls and ribbed plates, so every island takes the sheet's reading. They arrived as skin, the monster profile's default (islands.py never reads sheet_materials).",
